    \textbf{Case 2C: Condition \ref{bound_cond2} breaks at $J^\dagger+1$.}
        Now, assume without loss of generality that $J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 1\relax}}}\bigwedge J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 3\relax}}} \geq 1$. If this is not true, follow the relevant previous proof. Recall one final time that this implies $J^\star = J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 1\relax}}}$. Now we have $\delta^2_{J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 2\relax}}}} = \delta_{J^\dagger}^2 \geq \delta_{J^\star}^2 \vee \delta_{J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 3\relax}}}}^2$ which, with \Cref{lemma:delta_J_123_rates}, implies $\delta_{J^\star}^2 \gtrsim  \delta^2_{J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 2\relax}}}} \geq \delta_{J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 3\relax}}}}^2 \asymp \varepsilon^2\log^2(1/\varepsilon)$. This all gives us $\delta_{J^\star}^2 \asymp \delta_{J^{\operatorname{\uppercase\expandafter{\romannumeral 2\relax}}}}^2 \asymp \Upsilon^2/N \gtrsim \varepsilon^2\log^2(1/\varepsilon)$. Thus, we achieve our desired bound 
